The file testuser2EncodedJwt_Tamper.dat contains a base64 encoded JWT where
the body has been modified but the signature has not.
The encoded JWT should decode (without verification) to this:
HEADER:
{
  "alg": "RS256",
  "typ": "JWT"
}
BODY:
{
  "jti": "84b33dfb-b838-47c1-b57d-cc57b062042c",
  "iss": "https://dev.develop.tapis.io/v3/tokens",
  "sub": "testuser3@dev",
  "tapis/tenant_id": "dev",
  "tapis/token_type": "access",
  "tapis/delegation": false,
  "tapis/delegation_sub": null,
  "tapis/username": "testuser2",
  "tapis/account_type": "user",
  "exp": 1866806145
}

Note that the "sub" has been modified from "testuser2@dev" to "testuser3@dev"

The encoded JWT should fail verification.